# Code generated by project-standards. DO NOT EDIT.
#
# The universal .dockerignore every project shares, whatever its languages. It
# keeps repository metadata, local state and build output out of the image
# build context. Add a project's own entries under ignore.docker in
# mklv.config.json; the conformance bot appends them below and rewrites this
# file every week.

# Repository and CI metadata. Docker still reads the Dockerfile and this file.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# OS and editor files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode

# Environment files and unencrypted secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local
secrets/*
!secrets/*.sops.json

# Dependencies, caches and build output, which the image builds for itself
**/node_modules
**/.deno
**/.cache
**/.vite
**/dist
**/dist-ssr

# Tests, coverage and scratch files
**/coverage
**/*.out
**/*.coverprofile
**/*.test
**/*.log
**/tmp

# OpenTofu and Terraform
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
